1
00:00:01,139 --> 00:00:05,637
-(insects chittering)
-(birds chirping)

2
00:00:07,095 --> 00:00:09,220
We'll be starting the
Event in one minute!

3
00:00:09,303 --> 00:00:11,470
But, before we begin,
let's hear a few words

4
00:00:11,553 --> 00:00:14,385
of well-appreciated
encouragement

5
00:00:14,469 --> 00:00:16,469
from the always-eloquent
Utahime Iori!

6
00:00:16,552 --> 00:00:17,468
What? Huh?

7
00:00:17,551 --> 00:00:22,092
Well, I, uh, guess, uh,

8
00:00:22,176 --> 00:00:23,842
although during this Event

9
00:00:23,925 --> 00:00:26,134
some degree of injury
will be unavoidable,

10
00:00:26,217 --> 00:00:28,841
you should, uh, uh,
uh, help each other out,

11
00:00:28,924 --> 00:00:31,882
or something,
(chuckling) if you can?

12
00:00:31,965 --> 00:00:33,631
[Gojou] Okay, sorry, time's up!

13
00:00:33,715 --> 00:00:36,506
[Utahime] Ugh, Gojou
you jerk, I wasn't done!

14
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:40,672
[Gojou] Now, let the sister
school Exchange Event begin!

15
00:00:40,755 --> 00:00:43,172
-(feedback squeaking)
-(energetic music)

16
00:00:43,254 --> 00:00:45,463
[Utahime] You should
respect your seniors!

17
00:00:45,546 --> 00:00:46,546
Ichiro?

18
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:47,628
So stupid.

19
00:00:48,753 --> 00:00:49,336
Where did Toudou go?

20
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:51,670
How the hell should I know?

21
00:00:51,753 --> 00:00:52,544
I'm not his babysitter!

22
00:00:52,627 --> 00:00:54,961
[Kasumi] Can't we
all just get along?

23
00:00:55,044 --> 00:00:58,877
(energetic rock music)

24
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:03,959
-(insects chittering)
-(birds chirping)

25
00:01:04,042 --> 00:01:06,333
Where do you think
the cursed spirit boss is?

26
00:01:06,417 --> 00:01:08,499
It was probably
unleashed at the midpoint

27
00:01:08,583 --> 00:01:09,916
between the two groups,

28
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,707
but we can't expect
it to stand still.

29
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:14,915
At the pre-arranged
time, we'll all split

30
00:01:14,999 --> 00:01:16,639
into the Megumi Squad
and the Panda Squad.

31
00:01:17,956 --> 00:01:18,497
After that, it's on you.

32
00:01:18,581 --> 00:01:20,289
Got it, Yuuji.

33
00:01:20,372 --> 00:01:21,372
Got it!

34
00:01:23,788 --> 00:01:25,122
(Demon Dog barking)

35
00:01:25,205 --> 00:01:26,538
(creature chittering)

36
00:01:26,621 --> 00:01:30,121
(creature babbling)

37
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:31,745
Just small fry.

38
00:01:31,829 --> 00:01:35,078
(air whooshing)

39
00:01:35,162 --> 00:01:35,661
(Demon Dog snarling)

40
00:01:35,744 --> 00:01:37,285
Zen'in, stop running!

41
00:01:37,368 --> 00:01:40,577
(creature chittering)

42
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:45,576
-(blow booming)
-(Toudou yelling)

43
00:01:46,451 --> 00:01:48,408
Yeah, you're all together!

44
00:01:48,491 --> 00:01:52,158
Now come at me, all at once!

45
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,591
-(Yuuji grunting)
-(footsteps thudding)

46
00:01:53,615 --> 00:01:54,532
-(Toudou grunting)
-(Yuuji grunting)

47
00:01:54,615 --> 00:01:55,532
-(blow crashing)
-(Yuuji grunting)

48
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:57,406
[Maki] Scatter!

49
00:01:57,489 --> 00:02:00,531
(footsteps thudding)

50
00:02:00,614 --> 00:02:03,197
I wonder why Toudou was alone.

51
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,738
I'm not too sure,
but we were right

52
00:02:04,822 --> 00:02:06,030
to give Yuuji that job.

53
00:02:09,487 --> 00:02:12,778
He is a monster,
that much is for sure.

54
00:02:12,862 --> 00:02:13,778
Yup!

55
00:02:13,862 --> 00:02:15,778
But don't worry about him now.

56
00:02:15,862 --> 00:02:16,778
[Toge] Tuna.

57
00:02:16,862 --> 00:02:17,777
(both grunting)

58
00:02:17,861 --> 00:02:18,527
-(blow booming)
-(both grunting)

59
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:20,777
-(both thudding)
-(both grunting)

60
00:02:20,861 --> 00:02:23,609
(Toudou chuckling)

61
00:02:27,859 --> 00:02:30,733
(opening theme music)

62
00:02:33,315 --> 00:02:36,816
(singer singing in Japanese)

63
00:03:59,590 --> 00:04:03,297
Toudou will definitely be
out to crush us right away,

64
00:04:04,881 --> 00:04:07,630
and Mai might just follow
him in order to get to me.

65
00:04:07,713 --> 00:04:09,463
(air whooshing)

66
00:04:09,547 --> 00:04:10,839
Toudou is a monster.

67
00:04:10,922 --> 00:04:12,255
(body crashing)

68
00:04:12,338 --> 00:04:14,879
The worst possible outcome
would be that we all face him

69
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:15,963
and we all get wiped out.

70
00:04:16,629 --> 00:04:18,711
(air whooshing)

71
00:04:18,795 --> 00:04:21,878
So our plan was to leave
one of us, not sure who,

72
00:04:21,962 --> 00:04:23,841
either Panda or Megumi,
behind to deal with him.

73
00:04:25,961 --> 00:04:29,043
So now, Itadori, we'll
leave that role to you.

74
00:04:29,127 --> 00:04:30,584
[Yuuji] Hm?

75
00:04:30,668 --> 00:04:32,587
We can't afford to lose
any of our better scouts.

76
00:04:34,417 --> 00:04:35,667
You don't have to beat him,

77
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:38,833
just try to hold out
and buy us some time.

78
00:04:38,916 --> 00:04:40,416
I say be daring against him!

79
00:04:40,499 --> 00:04:43,040
To be blunt, we weren't
counting on your abilities anyway,

80
00:04:43,124 --> 00:04:45,665
so it won't matter too
much if you have to quit.

81
00:04:45,748 --> 00:04:47,580
Oh, thanks a lot!

82
00:04:47,664 --> 00:04:51,872
I'm sorry, Megumi, I know
you wanted to take on Toudou.

83
00:04:52,704 --> 00:04:54,663
No, I'm fine either way.

84
00:04:54,746 --> 00:04:56,329
[Panda] You're super low-key.

85
00:04:58,203 --> 00:05:01,245
I'll play along, if
you want me to.

86
00:05:01,328 --> 00:05:02,744
-Hm?
-Huh?

87
00:05:02,828 --> 00:05:04,244
And I'll win too.

88
00:05:04,327 --> 00:05:05,702
(pensive rock music)

89
00:05:05,786 --> 00:05:07,868
(Toudou growling)

90
00:05:07,952 --> 00:05:08,868
(Toudou spitting)

91
00:05:08,952 --> 00:05:10,868
At least your speed's decent.

92
00:05:10,952 --> 00:05:11,952
[Yuuji] Seriously?

93
00:05:11,993 --> 00:05:13,867
I thought I landed a good one!

94
00:05:13,951 --> 00:05:14,534
(energetic rock music)

95
00:05:14,617 --> 00:05:17,616
(Toudou grunting)

96
00:05:17,699 --> 00:05:20,866
(knuckles cracking)

97
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:22,532
So I'll return the favor!

98
00:05:22,615 --> 00:05:24,281
Act like your life's at stake!

99
00:05:25,532 --> 00:05:26,448
(Yuuji grunting)

100
00:05:26,532 --> 00:05:27,864
(creature chittering)

101
00:05:27,948 --> 00:05:29,239
(Toudou grunting)

102
00:05:29,322 --> 00:05:29,697
-(blow crashing)
-(Toudou yelling)

103
00:05:29,781 --> 00:05:32,239
(Yuuji grunting)

104
00:05:32,322 --> 00:05:34,780
(tree booming)

105
00:05:35,655 --> 00:05:40,529
-(Yuuji crashing)
-(Yuuji groaning)

106
00:05:42,362 --> 00:05:43,945
[Yuuji] My arm's still attached?

107
00:05:44,028 --> 00:05:44,611
(Yuuji gagging)

108
00:05:44,694 --> 00:05:47,403
I thought it got blown off!

109
00:05:47,486 --> 00:05:48,669
If that cursed spirit
hadn't gotten in the way,

110
00:05:48,693 --> 00:05:51,944
that would have been really bad!

111
00:05:52,027 --> 00:05:54,526
(Yuuji groaning)

112
00:05:54,609 --> 00:05:57,484
-(Yuuji gasping)
-(foot stomping)

113
00:05:57,567 --> 00:06:01,109
-(foot stomping repeatedly)
-(Yuuji groaning)

114
00:06:01,191 --> 00:06:02,941
(Toudou chuckling)

115
00:06:03,024 --> 00:06:07,981
-(foot stomping repeatedly)
-(Yuuji groaning)

116
00:06:09,231 --> 00:06:11,107
-(Toudou grunting)
-(foot stomping)

117
00:06:11,189 --> 00:06:13,980
(Toudou chuckling)

118
00:06:15,271 --> 00:06:18,229
♪ Oh oh oh oh oh oh ♪

119
00:06:20,896 --> 00:06:23,728
-(insects chittering)
-(birds chirping)

120
00:06:23,812 --> 00:06:25,561
All done huh?

121
00:06:25,645 --> 00:06:27,727
-(Toudou grunting)
-(neck cracking)

122
00:06:27,811 --> 00:06:30,560
(Toudou chuckling)

123
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:35,143
I wonder which one I
should go after now?

124
00:06:35,851 --> 00:06:38,142
-(fingers scratching)
-(Toudou gasping)

125
00:06:38,225 --> 00:06:41,350
-(Toudou laughing)
-(energetic electronic music)

126
00:06:41,433 --> 00:06:42,933
Man, are you for real?

127
00:06:43,016 --> 00:06:45,599
(Yuuji groaning)

128
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:51,264
What gives you the right

129
00:06:51,348 --> 00:06:53,514
to just stomp all over
my head like that?

130
00:06:53,597 --> 00:06:56,972
What if you made me even
dumber than I already was?

131
00:06:58,097 --> 00:06:59,262
Don't worry about that.

132
00:06:59,346 --> 00:07:01,805
Takada says, "Men are perfect
when they're a little dumb,"

133
00:07:01,888 --> 00:07:03,678
and I have a
feeling she's right.

134
00:07:05,553 --> 00:07:06,470
Takada?

135
00:07:06,553 --> 00:07:08,427
I don't care about any idols!

136
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:09,302
Really?

137
00:07:09,386 --> 00:07:11,219
So you don't care
about idols, huh?

138
00:07:11,302 --> 00:07:13,218
Well, I bet you know who she is.

139
00:07:14,094 --> 00:07:15,254
What's your name, first-year?

140
00:07:15,885 --> 00:07:18,009
Yuuji Itadori.

141
00:07:18,093 --> 00:07:20,509
All right, Yuuji Itadori.

142
00:07:20,592 --> 00:07:22,800
I have one question
that I need to ask you.

143
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:24,800
(Toudou chuckling)

144
00:07:24,841 --> 00:07:26,633
What kind of woman is your type?

145
00:07:28,298 --> 00:07:29,840
Huh?

146
00:07:29,924 --> 00:07:31,548
Uh, you wanna know my type?

147
00:07:31,632 --> 00:07:34,172
Why would you be
asking me that now?

148
00:07:34,255 --> 00:07:37,838
Nevermind why, I'm
just evaluating you.

149
00:07:37,922 --> 00:07:38,963
Uh...

150
00:07:39,047 --> 00:07:41,380
Well, I don't get
why it's important,

151
00:07:41,463 --> 00:07:43,295
but I guess if I had to say,

152
00:07:46,921 --> 00:07:51,503
I like a tall woman with
a nice big ass, just sayin'.

153
00:07:52,586 --> 00:07:54,752
Like Jennifer Lawrence!

154
00:07:54,835 --> 00:07:56,502
(Toudou gasping)

155
00:07:56,585 --> 00:07:59,834
-(Toudou gasping)
-(gentle dramatic music)

156
00:07:59,918 --> 00:08:01,876
-Hey, Usiji!
-Yeah, I know!

157
00:08:01,959 --> 00:08:04,166
-I totally understand.
-Got my lunch money?

158
00:08:04,249 --> 00:08:06,267
-Yeah, it's my lunch money!
-He doesn't even like me.

159
00:08:06,291 --> 00:08:07,458
He won't talk to me.

160
00:08:07,541 --> 00:08:09,582
-(pages rustling)
-(gentle guitar music)

161
00:08:09,665 --> 00:08:12,248
You know what, this
new series is pretty good!

162
00:08:12,332 --> 00:08:13,498
Yeah?

163
00:08:13,581 --> 00:08:16,247
-(students chattering)
-My mom knows-

164
00:08:16,331 --> 00:08:17,247
Huh.

165
00:08:17,331 --> 00:08:19,747
[Student] I just wish
it would snow already.

166
00:08:19,830 --> 00:08:24,913
-(bell chiming)
-(students chattering)

167
00:08:24,996 --> 00:08:28,328
(footsteps thudding)

168
00:08:29,953 --> 00:08:31,233
I'm gonna tell
Takada I love her.

169
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:34,078
Huh? No, don't do that!

170
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:36,285
Then you'd be crying
on my shoulder for days

171
00:08:36,369 --> 00:08:37,702
and that would suck!

172
00:08:37,786 --> 00:08:39,785
Why are you assuming
I'll get rejected?

173
00:08:39,868 --> 00:08:42,618
(footsteps thudding)

174
00:08:42,701 --> 00:08:44,076
An even better question is

175
00:08:44,158 --> 00:08:46,283
why do you think
she'll say yes to you?

176
00:08:46,367 --> 00:08:48,240
I remember something
that Anne Sullivan said

177
00:08:48,324 --> 00:08:50,240
at one point to Helen Keller.

178
00:08:50,324 --> 00:08:52,240
She asked her, "What
fool thinks of defeat

179
00:08:52,324 --> 00:08:53,406
"before even trying?"

180
00:08:53,490 --> 00:08:54,490
So-

181
00:08:54,531 --> 00:08:57,032
Uh, that was Inoki?

182
00:08:57,115 --> 00:08:58,238
(paper tearing)

183
00:08:58,322 --> 00:09:01,572
I'm really sorry, but I'm
already in love with someone.

184
00:09:03,863 --> 00:09:07,654
(footsteps thudding)

185
00:09:11,362 --> 00:09:14,070
(Toudou sobbing)

186
00:09:18,735 --> 00:09:22,818
[Toudou] Any chance that
the 'someone' she loves is me?

187
00:09:22,902 --> 00:09:23,941
No, no chance at all, man.

188
00:09:26,984 --> 00:09:29,149
Come on, let's get some ramen.

189
00:09:32,191 --> 00:09:33,857
My treat, what do you say, bud?

190
00:09:35,815 --> 00:09:38,898
(footsteps thudding)

191
00:09:42,522 --> 00:09:45,146
(hand tapping)

192
00:09:45,229 --> 00:09:47,897
(Toudou sobbing)

193
00:09:50,228 --> 00:09:53,186
So you never lost to anyone
in your hometown, huh?

194
00:09:56,062 --> 00:10:00,310
You and I were destined to
be best friends like we are!

195
00:10:00,393 --> 00:10:02,602
Hold on, you just
learned my name!

196
00:10:02,685 --> 00:10:03,768
(air whooshing)

197
00:10:03,851 --> 00:10:06,142
Yeah, keep heading
the way you are.

198
00:10:06,225 --> 00:10:06,934
He's with Toudou though.

199
00:10:07,018 --> 00:10:07,934
Not a problem.

200
00:10:08,018 --> 00:10:10,767
He was the one who told
us to do what we want.

201
00:10:13,390 --> 00:10:14,223
-(air whooshing)
-(gunshot booming)

202
00:10:14,307 --> 00:10:18,723
-(gunshots booming)
-(suspenseful music)

203
00:10:20,015 --> 00:10:22,473
[Kasumi] New Shadow
Style, Simple Domain!

204
00:10:22,556 --> 00:10:25,138
-(air whooshing)
-(footsteps thudding)

205
00:10:25,221 --> 00:10:26,388
Quick Draw!

206
00:10:26,472 --> 00:10:30,929
-(sword whooshing)
-(Yuuji grunting)

207
00:10:31,721 --> 00:10:32,721
What reflexes!

208
00:10:32,804 --> 00:10:34,386
I mean, I know I hesitated,

209
00:10:34,470 --> 00:10:36,803
but my counter didn't
even scratch him!

210
00:10:36,887 --> 00:10:40,344
-(air whooshing)
-(Yuuji gasping)

211
00:10:40,427 --> 00:10:41,886
(energy whooshing)

212
00:10:41,969 --> 00:10:43,218
[Yuuji] I'm surrounded!

213
00:10:44,052 --> 00:10:45,718
Wait!

214
00:10:46,885 --> 00:10:48,165
Why does it feel like these guys

215
00:10:49,967 --> 00:10:52,759
(air whooshing)

216
00:10:52,842 --> 00:10:55,341
are actually trying to kill me?

217
00:10:55,424 --> 00:10:56,758
(hands clapping)

218
00:10:56,841 --> 00:10:57,716
(both gasping)

219
00:10:57,799 --> 00:11:00,340
(both gasping)

220
00:11:00,423 --> 00:11:01,423
What the hell?

221
00:11:02,381 --> 00:11:03,505
-Huh?
-Did Itadori and I

222
00:11:03,589 --> 00:11:05,213
just switch places?

223
00:11:07,255 --> 00:11:08,421
Hey.

224
00:11:08,504 --> 00:11:09,864
-(Toudou grunting)
-(blow thudding)

225
00:11:09,921 --> 00:11:13,920
Didn't I tell you I'd kill you
if you interfered with me?

226
00:11:14,004 --> 00:11:15,087
(scoffing) No, you didn't.

227
00:11:15,170 --> 00:11:18,836
You just said you'd kill us
if we ordered you around.

228
00:11:18,919 --> 00:11:20,919
Was that switch
Itadori's technique?

229
00:11:21,003 --> 00:11:22,252
Or was it Toudou's?

230
00:11:22,961 --> 00:11:24,835
[Toudou] Same thing!

231
00:11:24,918 --> 00:11:25,918
Now piss off!

232
00:11:26,002 --> 00:11:28,584
(tense music)

233
00:11:30,125 --> 00:11:33,167
(footsteps thudding)

234
00:11:34,458 --> 00:11:35,541
He's retreating.

235
00:11:35,624 --> 00:11:36,124
How lame.

236
00:11:36,207 --> 00:11:37,833
[Kasumi] Thank goodness!

237
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:40,582
Make sure you kill him.

238
00:11:41,749 --> 00:11:43,058
I'd say all that
depends on Itadori.

239
00:11:43,082 --> 00:11:45,831
And quit givin' orders!

240
00:11:45,914 --> 00:11:46,748
[Yuuji] What's
with these people?

241
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:47,748
Trying to kill me

242
00:11:47,831 --> 00:11:49,788
and then arguing with
each other about it?

243
00:11:52,121 --> 00:11:54,412
It's lucky for you I'm
not an inconsiderate type

244
00:11:54,495 --> 00:11:58,079
who'd ever hold back against
his best friend in a fight!

245
00:11:58,162 --> 00:12:00,745
(air whooshing)

246
00:12:02,995 --> 00:12:05,243
(Momo groaning)

247
00:12:05,327 --> 00:12:08,576
This is why I said they
ought to leave him be.

248
00:12:08,659 --> 00:12:09,868
We're off to a bad start.

249
00:12:11,159 --> 00:12:13,409
We can't start hunting
down cursed spirits

250
00:12:13,491 --> 00:12:15,575
without me scouting
from the air either.

251
00:12:15,658 --> 00:12:17,034
(Momo sighing)

252
00:12:17,116 --> 00:12:18,907
They're all just so annoying!

253
00:12:21,074 --> 00:12:22,834
But hang in there, me,
you're the cutest one!

254
00:12:22,866 --> 00:12:25,197
Go get her!

255
00:12:25,281 --> 00:12:26,032
(electricity crackling)

256
00:12:26,114 --> 00:12:27,032
Oh.

257
00:12:27,114 --> 00:12:28,864
(electricity crackling)

258
00:12:28,947 --> 00:12:32,989
Mai, Mechamaru,
go help Nishimiya!

259
00:12:33,072 --> 00:12:34,071
[Mechamaru] Right.

260
00:12:34,154 --> 00:12:36,279
Yeah, we're in big trouble
without our air cover!

261
00:12:36,362 --> 00:12:41,070
-(footsteps thundering)
-(suspenseful music)

262
00:12:41,153 --> 00:12:42,611
(Kasumi gasping)

263
00:12:42,695 --> 00:12:45,485
-(weapons clanging)
-(both grunting)

264
00:12:45,569 --> 00:12:46,986
(Megumi and Noritoshi grunting)

265
00:12:47,069 --> 00:12:48,277
(both grunting)

266
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:53,318
Kamo is your team
trying to kill Yuuji Itadori?

267
00:12:57,984 --> 00:13:00,357
(energetic music)

268
00:13:03,566 --> 00:13:06,106
(frantic music)

269
00:13:08,605 --> 00:13:11,897
-(wind whooshing)
-(birds chirping)

270
00:13:11,981 --> 00:13:12,981
It's odd.

271
00:13:13,023 --> 00:13:14,646
This is strange.

272
00:13:14,730 --> 00:13:16,855
All the Kyoto students
are moving together.

273
00:13:18,187 --> 00:13:20,270
They're heading for
where we left Yuuji.

274
00:13:20,353 --> 00:13:22,979
It would seem unlikely
that that's a coincidence.

275
00:13:23,062 --> 00:13:26,519
Aren't they just headed
toward the cursed spirit?

276
00:13:26,602 --> 00:13:27,477
No way.

277
00:13:27,561 --> 00:13:29,935
Unless the special-grade
is especially cunning,

278
00:13:30,019 --> 00:13:31,643
Demon Dog would've sensed it.

279
00:13:31,727 --> 00:13:33,560
(Demon Dog barking)

280
00:13:33,643 --> 00:13:34,934
You think...

281
00:13:35,018 --> 00:13:37,684
Could they be
trying to kill Itadori?

282
00:13:37,767 --> 00:13:38,683
What the hell?

283
00:13:38,766 --> 00:13:39,683
How can that be?

284
00:13:39,766 --> 00:13:41,933
(tense music)

285
00:13:44,557 --> 00:13:45,557
It could be.

286
00:13:46,724 --> 00:13:47,890
[Toge] Kelp.

287
00:13:47,974 --> 00:13:50,139
I didn't sense that
level of hostility

288
00:13:50,222 --> 00:13:51,342
from them when they arrived,

289
00:13:51,389 --> 00:13:54,805
but that was before we
found out Yuuji was still alive.

290
00:13:54,888 --> 00:13:55,221
(Nobara gasping)

291
00:13:55,305 --> 00:13:57,513
(flute trilling)

292
00:13:57,596 --> 00:14:00,137
It is conceivable that
Principal Gakuganji

293
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:01,804
would order this move.

294
00:14:01,887 --> 00:14:03,071
So are the Kyoto
students all such cowards

295
00:14:03,095 --> 00:14:05,012
they kill on someone's orders?

296
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:07,678
That's pathetic.

297
00:14:07,761 --> 00:14:09,302
You have to realize
that they don't

298
00:14:09,385 --> 00:14:10,969
see Yuuji the way you do.

299
00:14:11,052 --> 00:14:13,801
The two of you have spent
day after day with him.

300
00:14:13,884 --> 00:14:15,801
We've just become
familiar with him.

301
00:14:15,884 --> 00:14:17,175
He's a good person.

302
00:14:17,259 --> 00:14:20,050
I'd say he's happier than
most sorcerers I've known.

303
00:14:20,133 --> 00:14:21,133
But still,

304
00:14:22,425 --> 00:14:24,066
for those who don't
know anything about Yuuji,

305
00:14:24,090 --> 00:14:27,340
just the fact that he's
the vessel of Sukuna

306
00:14:27,424 --> 00:14:30,131
makes him an object of fear.

307
00:14:30,214 --> 00:14:31,941
So for them, killing him
wouldn't feel any different

308
00:14:31,965 --> 00:14:34,505
than exorcizing a curse.

309
00:14:34,588 --> 00:14:36,839
Even for normal
jujutsu sorcerers,

310
00:14:36,922 --> 00:14:38,202
that line can
easily get blurred.

311
00:14:42,254 --> 00:14:45,586
[Maki] Megumi, we're
going back for him.

312
00:14:45,670 --> 00:14:46,378
I'm sorry.

313
00:14:46,461 --> 00:14:48,045
What are you
apologizing for, dummy?

314
00:14:49,085 --> 00:14:51,377
If you let a friend die,

315
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:53,836
winning or losing an
event doesn't matter.

316
00:14:55,626 --> 00:14:58,209
Yuuji's not answering
his phone anymore either.

317
00:14:58,293 --> 00:15:00,332
Nobara and I will go back
to confirm that he's safe.

318
00:15:02,458 --> 00:15:05,124
As for you, Toge, you keep
hunting the cursed spirit.

319
00:15:06,416 --> 00:15:07,541
[Toge] Bonito flakes.

320
00:15:07,624 --> 00:15:09,415
I know you're worried
about Yuuji too,

321
00:15:10,623 --> 00:15:13,081
but if my prediction
here is correct,

322
00:15:13,164 --> 00:15:16,706
the Kyoto students plan
here is to use the chaos

323
00:15:16,789 --> 00:15:19,955
and confusion of this
battle to assassinate Yuuji.

324
00:15:20,038 --> 00:15:23,413
Their attempts will end
as soon as the battle does.

325
00:15:23,496 --> 00:15:24,745
Makes sense.

326
00:15:24,829 --> 00:15:26,120
[Toge] Salmon.

327
00:15:26,203 --> 00:15:28,037
I'm worried about Maki too.

328
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,869
We won't let them kill Yuuji,

329
00:15:29,953 --> 00:15:31,744
and we're gonna win this fight!

330
00:15:31,828 --> 00:15:32,744
Copy that!

331
00:15:32,828 --> 00:15:34,618
(phone line beeping)

332
00:15:34,702 --> 00:15:35,702
Hm?

333
00:15:36,493 --> 00:15:37,743
(Nobara growling)

334
00:15:37,827 --> 00:15:40,034
Why don't you answer
your phone, Fushiguro?

335
00:15:40,117 --> 00:15:42,034
So lame!

336
00:15:42,117 --> 00:15:44,116
Why didn't they
give us wireless radios

337
00:15:44,199 --> 00:15:46,408
or at least Bluetooth earbuds?

338
00:15:46,491 --> 00:15:49,240
I don't like those
things, they're distracting!

339
00:15:49,323 --> 00:15:51,115
I get startled when
when calls come in.

340
00:15:51,198 --> 00:15:53,573
So then you just take
'em off during combat!

341
00:15:53,657 --> 00:15:54,739
(air whooshing)

342
00:15:54,823 --> 00:15:57,614
(Momo crashing)

343
00:15:57,698 --> 00:15:58,698
(Momo groaning)

344
00:15:58,739 --> 00:15:59,738
That hurt!

345
00:16:02,238 --> 00:16:04,696
So that's Fushiguro's Nue, huh?

346
00:16:05,529 --> 00:16:06,445
Electrified wings.

347
00:16:06,529 --> 00:16:09,444
That's gonna limit my
movement for a while.

348
00:16:09,528 --> 00:16:12,194
-(blow booming)
-(Momo grunting)

349
00:16:12,278 --> 00:16:17,277
♪ Nishimiya, there in a tree ♪

350
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:21,067
♪ Come down and play ♪

351
00:16:21,150 --> 00:16:21,985
[Momo] Ugh, how childish!

352
00:16:22,067 --> 00:16:24,900
That is not cute at all!

353
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:28,066
[Megumi] Kamo, are you
guys planning to kill Itadori?

354
00:16:28,149 --> 00:16:30,816
And if I said we were?

355
00:16:30,899 --> 00:16:32,607
What does it matter?

356
00:16:32,691 --> 00:16:34,123
It would mean
that you've all failed.

357
00:16:34,147 --> 00:16:37,606
Itadori could never be
defeated in such a short time.

358
00:16:42,272 --> 00:16:43,897
We've no reason to kill him.

359
00:16:44,771 --> 00:16:45,646
Yes, you do.

360
00:16:45,729 --> 00:16:48,062
The major three clans
and the higher-ups.

361
00:16:49,270 --> 00:16:54,227
-(blows booming)
-(birds chittering)

362
00:16:55,185 --> 00:16:58,102
-(both grunting)
-(blow thudding)

363
00:16:58,185 --> 00:17:03,101
-(blows thudding)
-(both grunting)

364
00:17:04,350 --> 00:17:06,934
-(blow thudding)
-(Yuuji grunting)

365
00:17:07,017 --> 00:17:09,141
-(punch thudding)
-(Yuuji grunting)

366
00:17:09,224 --> 00:17:11,182
-(kick thudding)
-(Yuuji yelling)

367
00:17:11,266 --> 00:17:13,641
-(blows thudding)
-(both grunting)

368
00:17:13,724 --> 00:17:17,139
-(Yuuji grunting)
-(energetic music)

369
00:17:17,223 --> 00:17:20,180
(Yuuji yelling)

370
00:17:20,264 --> 00:17:21,180
(Toudou grunting)

371
00:17:21,264 --> 00:17:22,055
Wow, what amazing toughness!

372
00:17:22,138 --> 00:17:24,513
He's actively
using the landscape

373
00:17:24,596 --> 00:17:26,054
to his advantage as well!

374
00:17:26,137 --> 00:17:27,513
(Toudou gasping)

375
00:17:27,596 --> 00:17:28,513
Where'd he go?

376
00:17:28,596 --> 00:17:29,845
(air whooshing)

377
00:17:29,929 --> 00:17:31,112
-(blow thudding)
-(Toudou grunting)

378
00:17:31,136 --> 00:17:34,136
He's also quick to
set up his next move!

379
00:17:34,219 --> 00:17:36,469
♪ Ah ah ah ♪

380
00:17:36,552 --> 00:17:41,343
-(blows thudding)
-(both grunting)

381
00:17:42,093 --> 00:17:43,093
And to top it off,

382
00:17:44,592 --> 00:17:45,217
-(punch booming)
-(Toudou grunting)

383
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:48,050
he has such tremendous power!

384
00:17:48,133 --> 00:17:49,967
His raw strength is
greater than mine,

385
00:17:50,049 --> 00:17:51,758
despite his smaller body!

386
00:17:51,841 --> 00:17:53,675
Which is why his
blows are still effective

387
00:17:53,758 --> 00:17:55,465
with so little cursed energy!

388
00:17:55,548 --> 00:17:57,465
And because there's
so little of that,

389
00:17:57,548 --> 00:17:59,131
it's hard to read his movements!

390
00:18:00,297 --> 00:18:02,337
But the way his cursed
energy hits after a time lag?

391
00:18:03,381 --> 00:18:06,797
Well, that is just
that's just, it's just

392
00:18:08,171 --> 00:18:09,213
Wrong!

393
00:18:09,295 --> 00:18:11,087
Wrong!

394
00:18:11,170 --> 00:18:12,712
Wrong!

395
00:18:12,796 --> 00:18:14,087
Wrong!

396
00:18:14,170 --> 00:18:15,711
Wrong!

397
00:18:15,795 --> 00:18:16,336
Wrong!

398
00:18:16,419 --> 00:18:18,503
Wrong!

399
00:18:18,586 --> 00:18:21,293
(leaves rustling)

400
00:18:23,585 --> 00:18:24,918
Was that Toudou yelling?

401
00:18:26,001 --> 00:18:27,292
Yeah, it was.

402
00:18:27,376 --> 00:18:30,541
Since he was up against
Yuuji, I'm starting to understand

403
00:18:30,625 --> 00:18:32,375
why you failed
to finish him off.

404
00:18:33,583 --> 00:18:36,749
So why'd you separate
from Noritoshi?

405
00:18:36,832 --> 00:18:39,165
Is your technique a
secret from your allies too?

406
00:18:41,081 --> 00:18:44,497
(sword rattling)

407
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:47,372
I am sorry about Itadori.

408
00:18:47,455 --> 00:18:50,162
Not to make excuses, but
I'm really not like the others.

409
00:18:52,162 --> 00:18:53,955
Still, that doesn't
mean I'm about to quit

410
00:18:54,037 --> 00:18:56,578
and just let you guys
win this Exchange Event!

411
00:18:56,662 --> 00:18:57,411
(upbeat music)

412
00:18:57,495 --> 00:18:59,911
You know that
sorcerers advance in rank

413
00:18:59,994 --> 00:19:02,452
through a recommendation
system, right?

414
00:19:02,535 --> 00:19:04,035
The Exchange Event
has always been

415
00:19:04,118 --> 00:19:05,368
a big deal to the sorcerers

416
00:19:05,451 --> 00:19:07,291
who don't have connections
higher up the chain.

417
00:19:07,326 --> 00:19:10,575
Students who perform well
here are granted many chances

418
00:19:10,659 --> 00:19:12,200
to advance while
they're studying.

419
00:19:15,115 --> 00:19:16,175
By rule though,
the person in charge

420
00:19:16,199 --> 00:19:19,366
of a student can't
recommend them.

421
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:21,281
For instance, Gojou can't give

422
00:19:21,365 --> 00:19:24,031
Yuuji Itadori a first-grade
recommendation.

423
00:19:24,448 --> 00:19:27,405
I want independence
as soon as possible,

424
00:19:27,489 --> 00:19:28,729
that way I can earn some money.

425
00:19:33,238 --> 00:19:34,238
[Maki] Why?

426
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:37,987
-(sword rattling)
-(tense music)

427
00:19:38,070 --> 00:19:38,528
Because I'm poor!

428
00:19:38,612 --> 00:19:40,277
And I'm the eldest.

429
00:19:40,361 --> 00:19:42,277
Yeah, but how about you?

430
00:19:42,361 --> 00:19:45,068
How do you tolerate Mai?

431
00:19:45,151 --> 00:19:46,235
You seem too nice.

432
00:19:46,318 --> 00:19:47,235
[Kasumi] What?

433
00:19:47,318 --> 00:19:48,318
Hm, yeah, I might be.

434
00:19:50,859 --> 00:19:52,234
I won't hold back, you know?

435
00:19:53,234 --> 00:19:55,566
That's not a problem!

436
00:19:55,650 --> 00:19:57,900
I didn't tell you all that
to get your sympathy!

437
00:20:01,023 --> 00:20:04,940
Listen, my friend, that
time-lagged cursed energy blast?

438
00:20:05,022 --> 00:20:06,207
That is a bad habit
you've developed.

439
00:20:06,231 --> 00:20:09,064
[Yuuji] Oh, you
mean Divergent Fist?

440
00:20:09,522 --> 00:20:10,438
What the hell?

441
00:20:10,521 --> 00:20:12,605
Where's he going with this?

442
00:20:13,897 --> 00:20:16,103
If you rely on
just that one trick,

443
00:20:16,187 --> 00:20:17,437
you'll never defeat me!

444
00:20:18,729 --> 00:20:20,978
And if you're satisfied
staying on that level,

445
00:20:21,061 --> 00:20:23,228
then sadly you and I can't
possibly stay best friends.

446
00:20:24,269 --> 00:20:26,602
You okay with that?

447
00:20:26,685 --> 00:20:29,477
I don't know, I
don't care about that.

448
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:31,976
[Toudou] You're okay
with staying weak?

449
00:20:32,059 --> 00:20:34,434
(Yuuji gasping)

450
00:20:34,517 --> 00:20:35,183
(energy whooshing)

451
00:20:35,266 --> 00:20:37,600
Definitely not!

452
00:20:37,683 --> 00:20:39,641
-♪ Oh oh oh oh oh oh ♪
-(tense music)

453
00:20:39,724 --> 00:20:41,974
That's more like it!

454
00:20:42,057 --> 00:20:44,265
My new best friend!

455
00:20:45,431 --> 00:20:48,598
(closing theme music)

456
00:20:55,596 --> 00:20:59,221
(singer singing in Japanese)

457
00:22:15,455 --> 00:22:17,455
-Juju Stroll!
-(playful music)

458
00:22:17,538 --> 00:22:19,455
(pensive music)

459
00:22:22,454 --> 00:22:23,704
At minimum?

460
00:22:23,787 --> 00:22:25,494
Someone who's
stronger than I am.

461
00:22:26,536 --> 00:22:27,953
Huh?

462
00:22:28,036 --> 00:22:30,744
What makes you think
I'd answer that question?

463
00:22:30,827 --> 00:22:33,577
I totally can't stand a UBSSD.

464
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:35,534
(playful digital music)

465
00:22:35,618 --> 00:22:37,910
You guys know who
Sebastian Stan is?

466
00:22:37,992 --> 00:22:38,534
(Momo giggling)

467
00:22:38,618 --> 00:22:41,575
His body is awesome!

468
00:22:41,658 --> 00:22:44,200
Well, of course I
naturally have a thing

469
00:22:44,283 --> 00:22:46,341
for hot-looking guys, just
the same as any girl would.

470
00:22:46,365 --> 00:22:50,698
But, in my mind, a guy has
to be fun to hang out with!

471
00:22:50,781 --> 00:22:53,573
And then, the most
important thing?

472
00:22:53,656 --> 00:22:55,363
Well, he should make you feel

473
00:22:55,447 --> 00:22:56,687
like he's the only one for you!

474
00:22:58,822 --> 00:22:59,906
(Kasumi gasping)

475
00:22:59,987 --> 00:23:02,571
(chuckling) Gosh, now I've
gone and embarrassed myself!

476
00:23:02,654 --> 00:23:05,570
Uh, wait, I know!

477
00:23:05,653 --> 00:23:08,612
I, ugh, I can't remember.

478
00:23:09,612 --> 00:23:11,777
Uh, hold on!

479
00:23:11,861 --> 00:23:13,402
You know, the girl who was nice?

480
00:23:13,485 --> 00:23:14,611
Uh, the nice girl!

481
00:23:14,694 --> 00:23:16,401
The girl who has the cool bangs?

482
00:23:16,484 --> 00:23:18,318
Yeah, you know her!

483
00:23:19,401 --> 00:23:20,442
Nice.

484
00:23:20,525 --> 00:23:21,525
Nice.

485
00:23:22,483 --> 00:23:23,483
Nice.

486
00:23:23,567 --> 00:23:25,941
(steady ticking)

487
00:23:26,024 --> 00:23:27,024
(beeping)

488
00:23:27,649 --> 00:23:29,316
(beeping)

489
00:23:31,023 --> 00:23:32,023
(beeping)

490
00:23:32,648 --> 00:23:34,315
(beeping)

491
00:23:36,022 --> 00:23:38,647
(bright chiming)

492
00:23:39,647 --> 00:23:40,521
(bell dinging)

493
00:23:40,605 --> 00:23:41,646
Oh! Miwa?

494
00:23:41,730 --> 00:23:43,646
Oh, yeah, that's her!

495
00:23:45,353 --> 00:23:49,854
(heavy metal music)

